{"at":"2026-02-16T23:09:33.041Z","userId":"admin","page":{"id":211,"status":"published","language":"en","path":"/docs/propertylist-mls-user-manual/how-to-use-the-calendar/managing-your-schedule-and-tasks/","title":"Managing your schedule and tasks • PropertyList Info Hub","description":"Managing your schedule effectively is crucial, especially when dealing with real estate. Let’s break down the steps for managing your schedule on PropertyList:Access the Calendar:Log in to your PropertyList.es account.On the left-hand side, click the “Calendar” tab. This will take you to your calendar view.Create a New Event:Once you’re in the calendar view, you have","body":"<div class=\"doc-post-content \" id=\"post\">\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"shortcode_title\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"ezd-doc-badge\" href=\"https://info.propertylist.es/docs/propertylist-mls-user-manual/how-to-use-the-calendar/\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tCalendar\t\t\t\t\t</a>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<h1>Managing your schedule and tasks</h1>\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"ezd-meta dot-sep\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"read-time\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tEstimated reading: 2 minutes\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"views sep\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t885 views\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t<div class=\"doc-scrollable editor-content\">\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t<div class=\"doc-content-wrap\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"10229\" class=\"elementor elementor-10229\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-72d0c7f e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"72d0c7f\" data-element_type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7bc3440 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"7bc3440\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"content user-select-text\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-description=\"\" aria-label=\"Sent by Copilot: Certainly! Let's create a step-by-step guide on how to manage your schedule using a calendar. Whether you're organizing work meetings, social events, or just keeping track of your day, having a well-managed calendar can make life a lot smoother. 😊 Here we go: 1. **Open Your Calendar**: - First, open your preferred calendar application. Since you're using Windows, you might be using the built-in Windows Calendar app or a third-party app like Microsoft Outlook or Google Calendar. 2. **Navigate to the Calendar Tab**: - Look for the &quot;Calendar&quot; tab on the left-hand side of your screen. It's usually represented by a calendar icon. Click on it to access your calendar view. 3. **Create a New Event**: - Once you're in the calendar view, find the option to create a new event. In most apps, this is either a button labeled &quot;New Event&quot; or an option to click directly on the time slot for the event you want to schedule. 4. **Event Details**: - Click on the desired time slot (or use the &quot;New Event&quot; button) to open the event details form. - You'll see fields where you can input information about the event: - **Title**: Either choose a preset title (like &quot;Meeting&quot; or &quot;Appointment&quot;) or add your own custom title. - **Start and End Time**: Set the start and end times for your event. If it's an all-day event, there's usually an option for that too. - **Location**: Specify where the event will take place (if applicable). - **Notes**: Write any relevant notes about the event. This could include an agenda, important details, or reminders. 5. **Invite Attendees (Agents)**: - If this event involves other people (such as colleagues, friends, or family), you can invite them. Look for an option like &quot;Add Attendees&quot; or &quot;Invite.&quot; - Enter the email addresses or names of the people you want to invite. Each attendee will receive a notification about the event. 6. **Set Reminders**: - It's essential to get timely reminders for your events. Choose when you want to be notified: - **Reminders Before the Event**: You can set reminders to go off a certain amount of time before the event starts (e.g., 15 minutes, 1 hour, etc.). 7. **Link a Property (MLS)**: - If this event is related to a property (perhaps a real estate showing), you can link it to the MLS (Multiple Listing Service) listing. This helps keep everything organized. - Look for an option like &quot;Link Property&quot; or &quot;MLS Reference.&quot; 8. **Link a Saved Contact**: - If the event involves someone you've previously saved in your contacts (like a client or a colleague), link their contact information to the event. - Search for the contact's name or email address and associate it with the event. 9. **Save the Event**: - Finally, click the &quot;Save&quot; button (or equivalent) to save the event to your calendar. - The event will now appear in your calendar view at the specified time. 10. **Review and Edit**: - After saving, take a moment to review the event details. If you need to make any changes, you can usually edit the event by clicking on it in your calendar. And there you have it! Your event is now scheduled and ready to go. Remember to check your calendar regularly to stay on top of your commitments. 🗓️✨ Feel free to ask if you need any further assistance or have additional questions! 😊 *Note: The specific steps may vary slightly depending on the calendar app you're using, but the general process remains consistent.* Is there anything else I can help you with?\"><div class=\"ac-container ac-adaptiveCard has-image\"><div class=\"ac-textBlock\"><div class=\"content user-select-text\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-description=\"\" aria-label=\"Sent by Copilot: Certainly! Managing your schedule effectively is crucial, especially when dealing with real estate. Let's break down the steps for managing your schedule on PropertyList.es: 1. **Access the Calendar:** - Log in to your PropertyList.es account. - On the left-hand side, click the &quot;Calendar&quot; tab. This will take you to your calendar view. 2. **Create a New Event:** - Once you're in the calendar view, you have two options: - **Option A: Click New Event** - Look for a button or link that says &quot;New Event&quot; (or something similar). Click it. - **Option B: Select a Time Slot** - Alternatively, you can click directly on the desired time slot on the calendar where you want to schedule an event. 3. **Event Details:** - You'll now be prompted to provide details for the event: - **Event Title:** - You can either choose from preset titles (if available) or create your own. Make it descriptive so you can easily identify the event later. - **Start and End Time:** - Specify the start and end time for the event. If it's an all-day event, there's usually an option to mark it as such. - **Event Note:** - Write any relevant notes about the event. For example, if it's a property showing, you might note the address or specific client details. - **Agents:** - Select the agent(s) who should be linked to this event. Each agent you select will receive notifications related to this event. - **Notifications:** - Decide when you want to be notified about this event (e.g., 15 minutes before, 1 hour before). - **Property Link:** - If the event is related to a specific property from the MLS (Multiple Listing Service), link it here. - **Contact Link:** - Link the event to a saved contact (e.g., client, buyer, seller). 4. **Save the Event:** - Once you've filled in all the necessary details, look for a &quot;Save&quot; button (usually at the bottom of the event form). - Click &quot;Save&quot; to add the event to your calendar. Remember, keeping your calendar organized and up-to-date is essential for successful real estate management. If you have any other questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask! 😊🏠🗓️ *Note: The instructions provided here are based on general principles for managing schedules and events. Specific steps may vary slightly depending on the exact interface and features of PropertyList.es.* Is there anything else I can assist you with?\"><div class=\"ac-container ac-adaptiveCard has-image\"><div class=\"ac-textBlock\"><p>Managing your schedule effectively is crucial, especially when dealing with real estate. Let’s break down the steps for managing your schedule on PropertyList:</p><p><strong>Access the Calendar:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: var(--p_color);\">Log in to your PropertyList.es account.</span></li><li>On the left-hand side, click the “Calendar” tab. This will take you to your calendar view.</li></ul><p><strong>Create a New Event:</strong><strong><br /></strong><span style=\"color: var(--p_color);\">Once you’re in the calendar view, you have two options</span></p><ul><li><strong>Option A: Click New Event<br /></strong>Look for a button or link that says “New Event”. Click it.</li><li><strong>Option B: Select a Time Slot<br /></strong>Alternatively, you can click directly on the desired time slot on the calendar where you want to schedule an event.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: var(--p_color);\">Event Details:</strong></p><p>You’ll now be prompted to provide details for the event:</p><p><strong>Event Title:<br /></strong>Make it descriptive so you can easily identify the event later.</p><ul><li><strong>Start and End Time:<br /></strong>Specify the start and end time for the event. If it’s an all-day event, mark it as such.</li><li><strong>Event Note:<br /></strong>Write any relevant notes about the event.</li><li><strong>Agents:<br /></strong>Assign the agent(s) who should be linked to this event. Each agent you select will receive notifications related to this event.</li><li><strong>Notifications:<br /></strong>Decide when you want to be notified about this event (e.g., 15 minutes before, 1 hour before).</li><li><strong>Add Property:<br /></strong>If the event is related to a specific property from the MLS, add it here.</li><li><strong>Add Contact:<br /></strong>Link the event to a saved contact (e.g., client, buyer, seller).</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: var(--p_color);\">Save the Event:</strong></p><ul><li>Once you’ve filled in all the necessary details, look for a “Save” button.</li><li>Click “Save” to add the event to your calendar.</li></ul><p> </p><p><span style=\"color: var(--p_color);\"><strong>Remember!</strong> Keeping your calendar organised and up-to-date is essential for successful real estate management. If you have any other questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask!</span></p><p> </p><p><em><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Note:</strong></span> The instructions here are based on general principles for managing schedules and events. Specific steps may vary slightly depending on the exact interface and features of <a role=\"link\" href=\"https://propertylist.es/?form=MG0AV3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-label=\"https://PropertyList.es\">PropertyList.es </a>in future updates. We strive to keep this information as current as possible. If you notice any discrepancies, please inform <a href=\"https://info.propertylist.es/docs/propertylist-mls-user-manual/additional-resources/mls-support/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">support.</a></em></p></div></div><div class=\"ad-container\"> </div></div></div></div></div>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\r\n\t\t\r\n\t</div>\r\n\t    <div class=\"doc-btm\">\r\n                <div class=\"eazydocs-next-prev-wrap\">\r\n\t\t\t                <a class=\"next-prev-pager second\" href=\"https://info.propertylist.es/docs/propertylist-mls-user-manual/how-to-use-the-calendar/syncing-your-calendar-with-other-apps/\">\r\n                    <span> Next - Calendar </span>\r\n